implementationPlan.description:
Tests, part 1 (the spelling rule and non-plain bases), one file: moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt.
- Change exactly one existing assertion. In 1c2bfeca's N11, the 'remote project' installedExecutable reason becomes "the project directory is not a plain local Windows path" (it was "the project directory cannot be resolved"); add a comment naming this row. Every other existing row stays byte-identical: N1-N12, S1-S9 and the rest.
- New rows take the next free names: N13, N14, S10 and S11 here, and S12 in step 3. N13 runs on every host. The others start with `assumeTrue("Windows path forms", RuntimeSelectionPolicy.windowsHost)` and must RUN on the verification host.
- Paths below are runtime spellings; write them as Kotlin literals with doubled backslashes.
- Install drive fakes only through the existing withDriveTargets, which restores the seam in finally (@After resetForTest does too).
- JNA works in this JVM through 1c2bfeca's jna.boot.library.path test setting. Add no other.

Helpers, placed next to share() and nonLocalSpellings():
1. nonLocalBases(project: File): List<String>. It is nonLocalSpellings(project) plus the following, with real = realFile(project).path and s = share("localhost", project):
   - s with '\' replaced by '/' (IntelliJ's `//localhost/X$/rest`);
   - `\\wsl$\moe-no-such-distro\proj` and `\\wsl.localhost\moe-no-such-distro\proj`;
   - `\\localhost\moe-no-such-share$\proj`, a missing share;
   - real.substring(2), the rooted form, and real.substring(0, 2) + real.substring(3), the drive-relative form;
   - `<real>\..\<project.name>`, `<real>\.`, `<real>.` and `<real> ` (JDK 17's Paths.get throws on the last one);
   - volumeSpelling(project) when it is not null.
   KDoc: the rule must refuse every one of these before any lookup.
2. rawJunction(link: File, target: String): Boolean. It makes a mount point on the new empty folder link whose substitute name is exactly `\??\` + target. Port it from D:\arch-52fb-r3-probe\Junction.java (rawJunction, proven on JDK 17.0.20):
   - link.mkdir();
   - Kernel32.INSTANCE.CreateFile(link.path, WinNT.GENERIC_WRITE, 0, null, WinNT.OPEN_EXISTING, WinNT.FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS or WinNT.FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT, null), refusing WinBase.INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE;
   - a com.sun.jna.Memory REPARSE_DATA_BUFFER: tag WinNT.IO_REPARSE_TAG_MOUNT_POINT, data length 8 + both names, the substitute name at offset 0, then the print name (target), each UTF-16LE and NUL-terminated;
   - Kernel32.INSTANCE.DeviceIoControl(handle, WinioctlUtil.FSCTL_SET_REPARSE_POINT, …, IntByReference(), null), with CloseHandle in finally.
   Any Exception or LinkageError answers false. KDoc: mklink /J and New-Item -ItemType Junction drop a trailing '.' from the target, so the reparse point is written directly; a mount point on an empty folder you own needs no privilege.
3. withDottedJunction(name, body: (link: File, dotted: String) -> T): T.
   - dotted = realFile(temporaryFolder.root).path + '\' + name + '.'.
   - Create it with exitOf("cmd", "/c", "mkdir", `\\?\` + dotted) and assert exit 0. Java's Paths.get rejects '?', and Win32 would drop the dot.
   - link = File(temporaryFolder.root, "$name-link"); assertTrue that rawJunction(link, dotted) succeeds; run body.
   - In finally, delete link (File.delete removes only the reparse point), then run exitOf("cmd", "/c", "rd", "/s", "/q", `\\?\` + dotted). TemporaryFolder cannot delete a dot-ending folder.

N13, pure predicate, every host. isPlainLocalPath(windows = true):
- is false for `C:\x\project.`, `C:\x\project.\bin`, `C:\x\project `, `C:\x\project \bin`, `C:\x\..\proj`, `C:\x\.\proj`, `C:\x\...`, `\\?\C:\x\project.` and `c:/x/project./bin`;
- is true for `C:\x\project.d\bin`, `C:\x\.hidden\bin`, `C:\x\a b\c` and `C:\x\v1.2.3`.
With windows = false, `/w/project.` and `/w/x/../y` stay true.

N14, isOutsideProject, Windows. Setup:
- project = newFolder("project") with bin/, and outside = newFolder("outside");
- store = ProtectedStateStore(temporaryFolder.root.toPath().resolve("system/moe/protected-state"));
- untouched = { throw AssertionError("looked up $it") }, an Error, so no catch swallows it.
Inside withDriveTargets({ throw AssertionError("drive mapping of $it") }):
- for every base in nonLocalBases(project) and every p in [project.path, bin, File(project, "missing").path, outside.path], assertFalse with resolve = untouched and with the default resolve;
- assertFalse(store.usableFor(base)), with a comment that this is the accepted cost: that project's protected state stays session-only;
- when volumeSpelling(project) is not null, isOutsideProject(outside.path, volumeBase, RuntimeProfile.LEGACY) is true. LEGACY never asks the seam.
Then, with the native seam:
- isOutsideProject(outside.path, project.path, resolve = { outside.toPath().resolve("nodejs.").resolve("bin") }) is false. It is a candidate real path with a dot segment; without the segment rule, identity would keep it.
- Controls: bin is not outside, outside.path is outside, and store.usableFor(project.path) is true.

S10, selection and spawn, Windows. Setup:
- (project, root, node) = protectedFixture();
- planted = File(project, "node"), containing "planted";
- sandbox = installedLayout(File(project, "build/idea-sandbox/plugins/moe-jetbrains"));
- volumeBase = volumeSpelling(project), guarded by assumeTrue(volumeBase != null) as S8 does;
- reason = BASE_NOT_PLAIN's text, and message = "Protected execution profile: $reason. Project and PATH copies of the Moe daemon are not used."
For every base in nonLocalBases(project), with the native seam:
- assertEquals(reason, assertRejected(…)) for installedExecutable(planted.path, base), installedExecutable(node.path, base), installedArtifact(sandbox, "daemon/index.js", base) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", base). The outside pair proves that the base check refuses, not identity.
- With PATH = node.parentFile.path, project.path and the project's bin, supervisorFor(project, { null }, { null }).protectedDaemonEnvironment(env, base) leaves mapOf("PATH" to "").
Spawn through volumeBase, which is local, so no SMB. For supervisorFor(File(volumeBase), { root }, { node.path }, started = started, statuses = statuses):
- ensureDaemonRunning() is false, started is empty, statuses == listOf(false to message) and selectionRefusal() == message;
- stopCommandOrNull(volumeBase) is null.
If ensureDaemonRunning cannot reach selection through the volume spelling (ensureMoeInitialized reads the project first), assert protectedDaemonCommand(volumeBase, root, node.path) == Refused(reason) instead, and say so in the step note.
LEGACY, inside withDriveTargets({ throw AssertionError("drive mapping of $it") }): supervisorFor(File(volumeBase), { root }, { node.path }, profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY }).stopCommandOrNull(volumeBase) equals listOf(realFile(node).path, realFile(File(root, "daemon/index.js")).path, "stop", "--project", volumeBase).
Control: installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) == Accepted(realFile(node)).

S11, a junction to a literal `project.`, Windows. Setup:
- (_, root, node) = protectedFixture();
- project = newFolder("project"), with File(project, "node") containing "planted";
- store as in N14;
- inside withDottedJunction("project"), write File(link, "node") with "node". It lands in `project.`.
Hazard, with a comment: File(dotted, "node").readText() is "planted". Read back, the real path opens the project's file.
Candidate side:
- installedExecutable(File(link, "node").path, project.path) is refused with exactly "node executable is not a plain local Windows path";
- isOutsideProject(link.path, project.path) is false.
Base side:
- installedExecutable(node.path, link.path) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", link.path) are refused with exactly BASE_NOT_PLAIN's text;
- isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, link.path) is false, and store.usableFor(link.path) is false.
Controls: installedExecutable(node.path, project.path) == Accepted(realFile(node)), and isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, project.path) is true.

No Gradle run is required in this step; step 3 runs RED and GREEN. A quick targeted run under the jetbrains-gradle lease is allowed.
Helper error handling: rawJunction never throws, and withDottedJunction always removes what it created, in finally.

Tests, part 2 (the drive seam on the base), plus RED and GREEN for every new check. Same file: moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/util/RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest.kt.

S12, a project on a drive letter that cannot be proved local, Windows. Setup:
- (project, root, node) = protectedFixture();
- native = RuntimeSelectionPolicy.windowsDriveTarget, captured first;
- untouched as in N14, asked = mutableListOf<String>() and store = newStore();
- reason and message as in S10.
Inside withSubst(project) { d -> … }, with base = the drive root (`"$d\\"` in Kotlin):
For each fake answer for the letter d:
- `\Device\LanmanRedirector\;<d>0000000000012345\srv\sh`, a mapped share;
- `\Device\Mup\srv\sh`;
- `\Device\ImDisk0`, a device family nothing proves local;
- null;
- one that throws IllegalStateException;
- one that throws UnsatisfiedLinkError, as when JNA cannot load.
Install it with withDriveTargets({ asked += it; if (it.equals(d, ignoreCase = true)) fake(it) else native(it) }) and assert:
- isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, base, resolve = untouched) is false, and store.usableFor(base) is false;
- installedExecutable(node.path, base) and installedArtifact(root, "daemon/index.js", base) are refused with exactly BASE_NOT_PLAIN's text. The node and root sit on a native drive, so their own preflights pass;
- supervisorFor(project, { null }, { null }).protectedDaemonEnvironment with PATH = node.parentFile.path and base gives mapOf("PATH" to "");
- for a fresh supervisorFor(File(base), { root }, { node.path }, started = started, statuses = statuses): ensureDaemonRunning() is false, started is empty, statuses == listOf(false to message) and selectionRefusal() == message.
LEGACY, with withDriveTargets({ throw AssertionError("drive mapping of $it") }):
- supervisorFor(File(base), { root }, { node.path }, profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY }).stopCommandOrNull(base) equals listOf(realFile(node).path, realFile(File(root, "daemon/index.js")).path, "stop", "--project", base);
- isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, base, RuntimeProfile.LEGACY) is true.
Controls with the native seam, on the same subst base: installedExecutable(node.path, base) == Accepted(realFile(node)), and isOutsideProject(node.parentFile.path, base) is true. 1c2bfeca's subst expansion proves the base local.
After the loop, asked is not empty and every entry matches `^[A-Za-z]:$`. The seam only ever gets a drive designator, never a UNC or a full path.

RED, then GREEN. Run each under the jetbrains-gradle lease: moe.acquire_resource just before, release right after, and never hold it across steps. Use: cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun --tests com.moe.util.RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest"
- RED-1: isPlainLocalBase answers true. N14, S10, S11's base side and S12 must fail.
- RED-2: isPlainLocalPath goes back to drive-qualified only. N13, N14, S10 and S11 must fail.
- RED-3: isPlainLocalBase skips the seam (spelling only). S12 and the renamed N11 assertion must fail.
- GREEN: restore everything and confirm the file matches your saved copy. The class passes, and N13, N14, S10, S11 and S12 executed without <skipped/>.
Record in the step note the rows each RED run failed, and the GREEN count. Afterwards `cmd.exe /d /c subst` lists no drive of yours.
If a peer's in-progress file breaks compilation, follow mem:gotcha-jetbrains-shared-tree-gate-peer-red, and never touch the peer's bytes.

Verification, run once.
- Take the jetbrains-gradle lease with moe.acquire_resource, and release it afterwards. If it is busy, release any lease you hold before you moe.report_blocked with that resourceId.
- WSL has no JDK. From a /mnt/d cwd, run exactly: cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun"
  This is DoD 2's gradlew.bat test, forced to run fresh.
- It must exit 0, and :test must execute (not UP-TO-DATE).
- In moe-jetbrains/build/test-results/test/TEST-*.xml, confirm:
  - failures=0 and errors=0;
  - this run stamped the RuntimeSelectionPolicyTest XML;
  - N13, N14, S10, S11 and S12 ran, without <skipped/>.
- Every existing row passes, unchanged except N11's one reason. In particular:
  - S1, S4, S8, PS4 and D1-D6;
  - 526a2080's N5-N7, S7 and S8;
  - 1c2bfeca's N8-N12 and S9;
  - all of MoeDaemonSupervisorTest, including W31-W35.
- Afterwards no `*-link` junction and no dot-ending folder is left under %TEMP%\junit*, and subst lists no drive of yours.
- Give complete_task the command, the exit code, the output tail and the test count, labelled as a Windows run.

Adversarial self-review of this diff only (git diff on the two files). Load adversarial-self-review. Check:
- Order. Read the final code. In both isOutsideProject and select, nothing touches the base before isPlainLocalBase(basePath): no Paths.get(basePath), realPathOrNull, isSameFile or physicalProject. The candidate resolver never runs for a refused base, and the seam only ever gets `X:`. N14's throwing seam and resolver and S12's recorder prove the candidate and drive sides; reading the code proves the base side.
- LEGACY. The new checks run iff strict(profile). Grep every caller of isOutsideProject, installedArtifact and installedExecutable. For each, state which profile it passes and what a non-plain base now yields. The callers are:
  - protectedPathEntries, via nodeOnProtectedPath and protectedDaemonEnvironment, for both the start env and stopBuilder's env;
  - ProtectedStateStore.usableFor;
  - installedDaemonCommand, via protectedCommandOrRefuse and stopCommandOrNull;
  - activationRefusal;
  - TerminalAgentLauncher.selectProtectedAgentRuntime;
  - ManagedVmPanel.nodeCommand.
  526a2080 was reopened exactly for missing the LEGACY Restart stop path. S10 and S12 pin it.
- Error handling. isPlainLocalBase fails closed through resolveWindowsDrivePath's catches, so a missing JNA refuses. isOutsideProject never throws; select returns Rejected.
- One JNA surface. This row adds no Kernel32 use, loader, seam or build setting in production. Test-only JNA stays inside rawJunction.
- POSIX does not change: isPlainLocalPath is true there and the seam is never asked. Plain local bases do not change either: every existing row passes.
- State the behavior changes:
  - under protected, a candidate whose normalized spelling or real path has a segment ending in '.' or ' ' is now refused;
  - a drive-qualified base whose mapping cannot be proved local now reads BASE_NOT_PLAIN instead of 'the project directory cannot be resolved' (N11);
  - on Windows under protected, a blank or relative base is now refused, where it used to resolve against the IDE's working directory.
- Refusal reasons carry no path, and there is no new shared state.
- The tests leave no junction, dot folder or subst drive behind.
- The diff touches exactly the two planned files, aiming at 300 net lines or fewer (1c2bfeca's handoff: its own budget is spent). Peer dirty paths stay untouched.
If this review changes any byte, re-run step 4's gate and report that fresh output.

The completion summary must give RF07 (task-f3f364a6):
- Accepted cost, under protected on Windows. A project opened through any of these starts nothing, keeps no PATH entry, and keeps its protected state session-only:
  - a UNC share, including \\localhost\C$;
  - a device path;
  - \\wsl$ or \\wsl.localhost;
  - a rooted or drive-relative spelling;
  - a '.', '..', trailing '.' or trailing ' ' spelling, or a base whose real path ends in '.';
  - a mapped network drive;
  - a drive on a device family 1c2bfeca does not recognize (VeraCrypt, ImDisk, WinFsp).
- TROUBLESHOOTING: clone to a local drive that is not mapped, run the IDE inside the distro for a WSL-hosted project, or stay on the legacy profile.
- Residuals, not fixed here:
  - RF02 and RF01 records are keyed by the spelling the project was opened through (projectKey). Tracking row 9a1da6f6 covers it.
  - A missing PATH leaf is compared lexically until dd545bf1 lands.
  - JetBrains refuses unknown device families; VS Code has no device-family check.

