- step 1(a)/(c): queryWindowsDriveType (Kernel32.GetDriveType) beside queryWindowsDriveTarget, a @Volatile windowsDriveType seam, LOCAL_DRIVE_TYPES, and isPlainLocalBase gated on the drive type;
- step 3: S12's DRIVE_REMOTE/UNKNOWN/NO_ROOT_DIR fakes, the default-GetDriveType assertion and RED-3;
- step 5: the "user-mode file system reporting DRIVE_FIXED is judged by identity only" residual.
A worker would get a plan that contradicts the governor's correction on this row.

Recommendation: send the row back to PLANNING, or amend_plan_step on steps 1, 3 and 5. It is unassigned, every step is PENDING, and it is gated on 1c2bfeca (step 3 IN_PROGRESS), so nothing is lost. Keep amendment (a) (no build.gradle.kts change), the raw-spelling-first order, and N9/N10/S10/S11. Change only the drive classification:
- 1c2bfeca's working tree already gates the base with the private unprovableDrive(basePath) (drive-qualified && resolveWindowsDrivePath == null, under strict(profile)) in isOutsideProject and select. In select it answers "the project directory cannot be resolved". Run that check right after the raw spelling rule with BASE_NOT_PLAIN, or relabel that branch. Add no GetDriveType.
- S12 fakes windowsDriveTarget instead: a \Device\LanmanRedirector or \Device\Mup target, an unknown device, null, a throw, and UnsatisfiedLinkError. Assert the seam only receives `X:`. RED-3 skips that check, and the DRIVE_FIXED residual goes.
If the governor keeps GetDriveType instead, comment-dfdb7239 needs an explicit retraction. Detail: msg-cc3e7435 in chan-b6d8273b.
